.Dd July 8, 2026
.Dt NEW_SYSTEM 8
.Os FreeBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm new_system
.Nd create a new system on top of an existing foundation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl s Ar name
.Op Fl f Ar foundation
.Op Fl o Ar key=value
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl b
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility creates a new system within the mishkan framework.
It sets up the minhag directory structure, provisions ZFS data
datasets, and records an inaugural git commit in the sinai
repository.
.Pp
A system is built on top of a foundation, which provides the
base archive for the root filesystem.
The
.Nm
utility creates a branch
.Pa system/ Ns Ar name
from
.Pa foundation/ Ns Ar name
in the sinai repository, writes
.Pa /etc/fstab ,
and leaves a zero-byte
.Pa .foundation
file as a reference to the originating foundation.
.Pp
Standard data-lake mounts for
.Pa var
and
.Pa usr/local
are always created.
Home and tmp datasets are optional and controlled via the
.Fl o
flag.
.Pp
Optionally,
.Nm
can deploy the newly created system to zbereshit via
.Xr deploy_system 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-f foundation"
.It Fl h
Display a help message and exit.
.It Fl d
Dry run.
Show what would be done without making any changes.
.It Fl s Ar name
Set the system name.
When omitted,
.Nm
runs in fully interactive mode and prompts for a name.
.It Fl f Ar foundation
Specify which foundation to base the system on.
.It Fl o Ar key=value
Set a property override.
This flag may be specified multiple times.
Available keys:
.Bl -tag -width "roothome_dataset" -compact
.It Cm home_dataset
Create a home dataset.
Default:
.Dq yes .
.It Cm tmp_dataset
Create a tmp dataset.
Default:
.Dq yes .
.It Cm roothome_dataset
Create a separate dataset for root's home directory.
Default:
.Dq no .
.It Cm user_homes
Comma-separated list of per-user home datasets to create.
.It Cm mount_map
Additional dataset-to-mountpoint mapping in
.Ar dataset:mountpoint
format.
May be specified multiple times.
.El
.It Fl q
Quiet mode.
Suppress interactive prompts.
May be specified twice:
.Fl q
suppresses prompts (property overrides or defaults are used);
.Fl qq
additionally suppresses progress output.
.It Fl b
Deploy the system after creation.
May be specified twice:
.Fl b
deploys to zbereshit;
.Fl bb
deploys and sets nextboot.
.El
.Sh MODES OF OPERATION
.Nm
supports three modes depending on which flags are supplied:
.Bl -tag -width "Semi-interactive"
.It Em Interactive
When
.Fl s
is not given, all questions are asked interactively.
.It Em Semi-interactive
When
.Fl s
is given but
.Fl q
is not, questions are still asked but values supplied via
.Fl o
serve as defaults.
.It Em Quiet
When both
.Fl s
and
.Fl q
are given, no prompts are issued.
All properties take their defaults or values supplied via
.Fl o .
.El
.Sh FSTAB
Two kinds of fstab are maintained:
.Bl -tag -width "recipe fstab"
.It Em "system fstab"
Contains normal filesystem mounts and is written to
.Pa /etc/fstab
within the system image.
.It Em "recipe fstab"
Contains container dependency mounts and is stored in
.Pa fstab.local
within the minhag system directory.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa minhag/systems/ Ns Ar name Ns /
Per-system configuration directory containing:
.Bl -tag -width "derivations.local" -compact
.It Pa .foundation
Zero-byte file recording the originating foundation name.
.It Pa compose.sh
System composition script.
.It Pa derivations.local
Local derivation overrides.
.It Pa fstab.local
Recipe fstab for container dependencies.
.It Pa mtree.dist
File hierarchy specification.
.It Pa pkg.list
Package list for the system.
.El
.It Pa zbamidbar/system-data/ Ns Ar name Ns /
ZFS data datasets for the system:
.Pa var ,
.Pa usr-local ,
.Pa home ,
.Pa tmp .
.It Pa zbamidbar/sinai.git
Bare git repository.
The system branch
.Pa system/ Ns Ar name
is created from
.Pa foundation/ Ns Ar name .
.It Pa zbamidbar/sinai.zfs/foundations/ Ns Ar foundation
ZFS dataset containing the source foundation archive.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a system interactively:
.Pp
.Dl # new_system
.Pp
Create a system named
.Dq webhost
on foundation
.Dq base14 :
.Pp
.Dl # new_system -s webhost -f base14
.Pp
Create a system quietly with no home dataset and deploy:
.Pp
.Dl # new_system -s webhost -f base14 -o home_dataset=no -q -b
.Pp
Dry run with custom user homes:
.Pp
.Dl # new_system -d -s webhost -f base14 -o user_homes=www,app
.Pp
Deploy and set nextboot:
.Pp
.Dl # new_system -s webhost -f base14 -q -bb
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr deploy_system 8 ,
.Xr new_container 8 ,
.Xr new_foundation 8
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
utility is part of the mishkan framework.
